KG42.register("clusters-f799f6e5f33a9929227cbc77",{"id":"30-motivational_game::v142-d-K001","paper":"30-motivational_game","label":"Peer-priority trading of solar surplus and CPS supplementation","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K001","label":"Peer-priority trading of solar surplus and CPS supplementation","market_meaning":"In the case of prosumers with rooftop PV without batteries, conditional on individual surplus or deficit, surplus electricity is first traded among peers, and remaining sales or purchases are then handled according to network surplus/deficit and CPS. The existing chain gives the product scope, individual priority order, and three network surplus/deficit outcomes, but per-household quantity allocation is not yet closed.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["bidding","clearing","activation"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"R001, R002's C004-C008, and R007 correspond to the same coalition trading case; R007's rooftop PV and no-battery limitations must be retained. R002's C001-C003 belong to general P2P description, and their full order-matching premise has not yet been aligned with the CPS residual-order handling in the case.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"Tradable surplus, peer-priority responsibility, and the destination of remaining electricity jointly constitute the allocation rule, and the product definition directly limits its input. Price calculation and post-matching payment procedures have separate independent responsibilities; different representations of the same priority principle in R001 and R002 are not counted as separate rules.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Undertakes the peer-priority allocation requirement on both the surplus and deficit sides, retaining the limitation on the deficit side that network-wide surplus is exhausted."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"C004-C008 supplement the individual execution branches and CPS surplus/deficit scenarios; C001-C003 retain their general descriptive scope, and the related interfaces are shared by reference in the performance cluster."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R007","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Limits the trading input to the solar surplus electricity of this no-battery rooftop PV case and retains the positive-surplus condition."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CN001","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e06","v141-b-g02-e07"],"rationale":"The same case first defines solar surplus and then specifies that it preferentially satisfies peer demand; product conditions and allocation responsibility are complementary, and this mapping does not add product nodes or quantity objects to R001."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CN002","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"alternative_representation","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06"],"rationale":"The two places express the seller's peer-priority principle in the same case, placed respectively under clearing and execution responsibilities; both the non-formalized formulation and the procedural expression are retained and are not counted as two independent rules."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CN003","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C005","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C008"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e07","v141-b-g03-e001","v141-b-g02-e18"],"rationale":"The individual first purchases energy from peers, and when the network has a deficit purchases supplementary energy from CPS, together with the network-wide surplus exhaustion limitation, describe the deficit-side responsibility; the specific limitations differ, so constraints cannot be declared completely equivalent on that basis, nor can new implication edges be added."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CN004","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R007::theta::v141-c-R007-theta-E_ns"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::theta_E_n_s"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e06"],"rationale":"Within the same rooftop PV case, the same prosumer, and the same time point, the product surplus and the trigger state of the execution branch point to the same source-text surplus; the local roles of product definition and execution input remain separate."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM001","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R007::theta::v141-c-R007-theta-E_ns","v141-c-R002::theta::theta_E_n_s"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e06"],"rationale":"The source-text definition and the contiguous case description support the correspondence of the same prosumer solar surplus; the basis is not limited to identical symbols. Preserve the two original parameters, product status and execution condition, together with their respective unspecified units."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM002","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06"],"rationale":"These can be associated as two representations of the same seller-priority principle, but one place has no expression, and the other marks the programmatic expression as source; the formalization source and equivalence still remain to be checked. Do not select a representative or rewrite the original."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-G001","category":"upstream_missing","description":"R001 has no approved surplus/deficit quantity object, allocated quantity, or edges for the two priority branches; referencing state quantities from other chains cannot supply its frozen graph, and per-household allocation and quantity conservation are also not yet closed.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e06","v141-b-g02-e07","v141-b-g03-e001"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream must clarify whether this chain serves only as a qualitative rule; if a complete allocation representation is required, the state quantities, priority branches and surplus interfaces of C.1 should be revised according to the source text, and then the C.2 binding updated. Unnamed transaction quantities cannot be introduced by D itself."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G002","category":"ontology_extension","description":"CPS surplus sale/purchase already has textual and scenario descriptions, but lacks a dedicated graph object representing external-grid surplus trading; v141-b-g01-EP02 remains a pending proposal and cannot be directly replaced by inter-area clearing.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C007","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C008"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E20","v141-b-g02-e07","v141-b-g02-e17","v141-b-g02-e18"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-EP02"],"required_work":"Handle the semantic boundary of this pending proposal; if upstream approval is obtained, C is then to express the external surplus sale/purchase relationship after peer trading; currently only the existing chain references are retained."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G003","category":"scope_conflict","description":"The all-peer-order matching threshold in the general description lacks an order-level connection with the peer supply-demand imbalance and CPS supplement in the case, so it cannot yet be concluded that all three surplus/deficit scenarios satisfy the execution precondition of R002-C001.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C007","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C008"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g02-e17","v141-b-g02-e18"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Determine clearly the set of orders covered by all matching, and how residual orders not satisfied by peers enter CPS trading; treatments not specified in the source text remain undecided, and no dependency edges are added from narrative order."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G004","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The formalization source of the two seller representations remains to be checked; the energy-deficit side R001 additionally contains a whole-network surplus exhaustion qualification, which is more specific than R002's individual priority energy-purchase formulation and cannot be collapsed as a completely duplicate constraint.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06","v141-b-g02-e07","v141-b-g03-e001"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the source-text scope, conditions and expression sources of each formulation; before upstream clarifies equivalence, retain the seller alternative representation and the buyer complementary qualification."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G005","category":"unverified_source","description":"The B evidence used by this cluster remains unverified; experimental candidate support eligibility does not mean that citation transcription, condition scope or scientific content has been independently verified.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e06","v141-b-g02-e07","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e17","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g03-e001"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Subsequently check the original text and conditions item by item, and inspect all assembly mappings; this round does not interpret candidate assembly as source or scientific endorsement."}]},"rule_refs":["30-motivational_game::v141-c-R001","30-motivational_game::v141-c-R002","30-motivational_game::v141-c-R007"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-189f5500ef3981fa","COMP-4cf3718d101da7ca","COMP-7112c31486848467","COMP-80c9b12d3ea35c91","KG40-a6a3b767e2722b06"]});
